abstract: >-
  VaxGuard is a decision-support tool for community health workers who must
  decide what to do with a vaccine after a cold chain break. It returns
  Usable, Hold or Discard from the vaccine vial monitor (VVM), a vial found
  frozen solid, and the WHO shake test, which is offered only for vaccine
  types where it has been validated. Mean kinetic temperature is shown for
  reporting and does not decide the verdict. It has 12 WHO EPI vaccine
  presets with sourced storage and handling data, and the interface is
  available in English, French, Swahili and Korean. The app runs entirely
  client-side as an installable, offline-capable Progressive Web App, with
  no login and no data collection by the app.